/- kdl-version 2

$element .title="About the museum — Atrium" .description="Atrium is the city's museum of art and history: a glass hall over the old customs house, free to enter, run by the city and its readers since 1897." {
    state {
        catalogued {
            $expression {
                operator call
                target (ref)"window#/Intl/formatNumber"
                value {
                    - 0.94
                    - #null
                    - style=percent
                }
            }
        }
        archive {
            $expression {
                operator call
                target (ref)"window#/Intl/formatNumber"
                value {
                    - 1240
                    - #null
                    - style=unit unit=meter unitDisplay=long
                }
            }
        }
        staff {
            $expression {
                operator call
                target (ref)"window#/Intl/formatNumber"
                value {
                    - 61
                }
            }
        }
        languages {
            $expression {
                operator call
                target (ref)"window#/Intl/formatList"
                value {
                    - English French Arabic
                }
            }
        }
    }
    mu-pagehead {
        $props {
            kicker About
            title "A museum that argues with itself"
            standfirst "Atrium was founded by 240 households who each put in what they could and demanded, in writing, that entry stay free. It has been kept that way for a hundred and twenty-nine years, through two rebuildings and one fire."
            metaLabel "Reading room"
            metaValue "Second floor, no appointment needed"
        }
    }
    mu-band {
        $props index="01" label="The building" tone=chalk
        div {
            style {
                display grid
                gridTemplateColumns "minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr)"
                columnGap "clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem)"
                rowGap "1.25rem"
                @--md gridTemplateColumns="minmax(0, 1fr)"
                alignItems start
            }
            div {
                style maxWidth="var(--measure)"
                p "The museum began in a room above the customs house, which it outgrew in nineteen years. The glass hall that replaced it in 1916 was built over the customs house rather than instead of it: the old stone walls are still standing inside, holding up nothing, and the tour begins by walking between them." {
                    style margin="0" lineHeight="1.75"
                }
                p "The roof is the reason people photograph the building and the reason the conservators dislike it. Every object on the ground floor is placed by how much light it can take, which is why the map cabinet sits in the darkest corner and the salt pan sits outside in the rain." {
                    style margin="1.1rem 0 0" lineHeight="1.75"
                }
                p "Nothing here is a copy. Where the museum shows a reproduction — three of the maps are too fragile to hang — the label says so in the first line, in the same size type as the title." {
                    style margin="1.1rem 0 0" lineHeight="1.75"
                }
                p "Where the museum does not know something, the label says that too. Roughly one object in nine has no attributed maker, and the catalogue records the gap rather than a guess." {
                    style margin="1.1rem 0 0" lineHeight="1.75"
                }
            }
            mu-oculus {
                $props size="20rem" tone=card
            }
        }
    }
    mu-band {
        $props index="02" label="What we hold" tone=card
        div {
            style {
                display grid
                gridTemplateColumns "repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr))"
                columnGap "clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem)"
                @--md gridTemplateColumns="minmax(0, 1fr)"
            }
            div {
                mu-fact {
                    $props {
                        term Catalogued
                        value "${state.catalogued}"
                        note "Of everything accessioned. The remainder is mostly the 2019 workshop bequest."
                    }
                }
                mu-fact {
                    $props {
                        term Archive
                        value "${state.archive}"
                        note "Of shelved paper: ledgers, survey notebooks, and workshop correspondence."
                    }
                }
            }
            div {
                mu-fact {
                    $props {
                        term Staff
                        value "${state.staff}"
                        note "Curators, conservators, front-of-house and the two people who keep the roof clean."
                    }
                }
                mu-fact {
                    $props {
                        term "Labels in"
                        value "${state.languages}"
                        note "Every wall label, every room, with no abridged version for any of the three."
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    mu-band {
        $props index="03" label="Three languages" tone=chalk
        div {
            style {
                display grid
                gridTemplateColumns "minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.85fr)"
                columnGap "clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem)"
                alignItems start
                @--md gridTemplateColumns="minmax(0, 1fr)" rowGap="2rem"
            }
            div {
                style maxWidth="var(--measure)"
                p "A third of this city reads French at home and a growing share reads Arabic, so the museum is written three times over rather than once with translations bolted on. Each language has its own pages, its own wall text and its own reading of the collection — the Arabic route through Gallery 2 is not the English one reversed, it is a different argument by a different curator." {
                    style margin="0" lineHeight="1.75"
                }
                p "Every page carries the same switch, and it lists only the languages that page actually exists in. If a language is missing from the switch, the page has not been written in it yet — that is a commitment we would rather show than hide." {
                    style margin="1.1rem 0 0" lineHeight="1.75"
                }
            }
            div {
                style {
                    border "2px solid var(--color-ink)"
                    backgroundColor "var(--color-card)"
                    padding "clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.9rem)"
                }
                p "This page, in every language it exists in" {
                    style {
                        margin "0 0 1.1rem"
                        fontFamily "var(--font-label)"
                        fontSize "0.66rem"
                        letterSpacing "var(--label-tracking)"
                        textTransform "var(--label-case)"
                        color "var(--color-muted)"
                    }
                }
                ul {
                    style listStyle=none margin="0" padding="0" display=grid gap="0.55rem"
                    .children {
                        $array items=(ref)"#/state/$page/alternates" {
                            li {
                                a .lang="${item.code}" dir="${item.dir}" href="${item.url}" hreflang="${item.code}" aria-current="${item.current ? 'page' : 'false'}" {
                                    style {
                                        display flex
                                        alignItems baseline
                                        gap "0.7rem"
                                        textDecoration none
                                        paddingBlock "0.35rem"
                                        borderBlockEnd "1px solid var(--color-hairline)"
                                        color "${item.current ? 'var(--color-muted)' : 'var(--color-pigment)'}"
                                        :hover color="var(--color-ink)"
                                    }
                                    span "${item.code}" {
                                        style {
                                            fontFamily "var(--font-label)"
                                            fontSize "0.64rem"
                                            letterSpacing "var(--label-tracking)"
                                            textTransform "var(--label-case)"
                                            opacity "0.7"
                                        }
                                    }
                                    span "${item.label}" {
                                        style fontSize="1.02rem"
                                    }
                                    span "You are here" {
                                        style {
                                            marginInlineStart auto
                                            fontFamily "var(--font-label)"
                                            fontSize "0.62rem"
                                            letterSpacing "var(--label-tracking)"
                                            textTransform "var(--label-case)"
                                            display "${item.current ? 'inline' : 'none'}"
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    mu-band {
        $props index="04" label="In the founders' words" tone=ink
        mu-quote {
            $props {
                quote "Let it be free at the door, or let it be something other than ours."
                attribution "Subscription minute book, 4 November 1897"
            }
        }
    }
    mu-cta {
        $props {
            kicker "Come in"
            heading "The reading room is open to anyone with a question."
            text "Second floor, above the map cabinet. No appointment to read; ask at the desk to handle."
            label "Plan your visit"
            href "/visit/"
        }
    }
}
